# UI & Design Rules — Cal.com Clone

## Non-negotiable
Every screen must closely match **Cal.com** (https://cal.com) in layout, spacing, typography, and interaction patterns. Evaluators demo the booking flow first — visual similarity matters as much as functionality.

Study Cal.com before building any UI. No generic dashboard aesthetics. No dev/debug copy in production UI.

## Stack
- **shadcn/ui** for primitives (Button, Calendar, Dialog, Input, Select) — never hand-roll primitives
- **Tailwind CSS** only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- **lucide-react** for icons — one library only
- **Inter** font (or Geist if already scaffolded) — `text-sm` body, clear hierarchy

## Cal.com color & spacing
- Page backgrounds: `bg-gray-50` (admin) / `bg-white` (public booking)
- Cards: `bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg`
- Headings: `text-gray-900` · secondary: `text-gray-500` · muted: `text-gray-400`
- Primary actions: dark/black button (`bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-800`) — Cal.com uses near-black, not bright blue
- Generous whitespace: `p-4` / `p-6` / `gap-4` / `gap-6`

## Page-specific patterns (must implement)

### Admin shell
- Left sidebar: Event Types | Availability | Bookings
- Active nav: `bg-gray-100 rounded-md font-medium` with icon + label
- Top area: app name + host name
- Content area on `bg-gray-50`

### Event types (`/event-types`)
- Card list (not a plain table)
- Each card: **colored dot** accent, **duration badge** (e.g. `30m`), title, slug subtitle
- Hover reveals copy-link / edit / delete actions
- "New event type" as primary dark button

### Availability (`/availability`)
- Timezone select at top
- **7-row weekly grid**: toggle per day + start/end time inputs (`09:00`–`17:00`)
- Not free-text — structured time pickers

### Public booking (`/book/[slug]`) — highest priority
- **3-column layout** on desktop:
  1. **Left** — host avatar/name, event title, duration, description
  2. **Middle** — month calendar (react-day-picker / shadcn Calendar)
  3. **Right** — time slot buttons (12h format, e.g. `9:00 AM`), then inline name/email form on slot select
- Dividers between columns (`border-r border-gray-200`)
- Mobile: stack columns vertically (info → calendar → slots)
- Slot buttons: full-width outline, `hover:border-gray-900`
- Confirmation page: summary card with date, time, event details

### Bookings dashboard (`/bookings`)
- Tabs: Upcoming | Past
- Clean table or list rows with cancel on upcoming confirmed

## Interaction rules
- All async buttons show loading state (spinner or disabled)
- Empty states: helpful message + CTA — never blank screens
- Forms: field-level validation errors
- 409 slot-taken: user-friendly message + refresh slots
- No placeholder text like "Module 1.6" or "connected to API" in UI

## Responsive
- Mobile-first; booking page must work on phone
- Sidebar → collapsible/hamburger on small screens
